@model Stanza.ControlPlane.Configuration.AgentPolicyEditor
@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Agent runtime policy"; }
<h1>Agent runtime policy</h1><p class="muted">Commands are accepted only through the authenticated approved-Agent channel. Docker socket access is effectively host administration.</p>
<section class="panel"><form method="post" class="form-grid"><div asp-validation-summary="All" class="validation"></div><input name="version" type="hidden" value="@Model.Version" />
<label class="check-field span-full"><input name="executionEnabled" type="checkbox" value="true" checked="@Model.Policy.ExecutionEnabled" /> Enable workload execution</label><input name="executionEnabled" type="hidden" value="false" />
<p>Operation timeout is configured globally in <a href="/settings#operations">Settings</a> and applies to every Agent. Output is recorded without a character limit.</p>
<label class="field">Concurrent workloads<input name="maximumParallelOperations" type="number" min="1" max="64" value="@Model.Policy.MaximumParallelOperations" required /><span class="field-help">Default: 1. Different deployments may run concurrently up to this limit. Each deployment permits one workflow at a time. Host-wide scripts run exclusively.</span></label>
<label class="field">Concurrent discovery requests<input name="maximumParallelDiscovery" type="number" min="1" max="64" value="@Model.Policy.MaximumParallelDiscovery" required /><span class="field-help">Default: 4. Git/registry discovery and read-only inspections use separate capacity, not workload slots.</span></label>
<label class="field">Discovery timeout (seconds)<input name="discoveryTimeoutSeconds" type="number" min="1" max="604800" value="@Model.Policy.DiscoveryTimeoutSeconds" required /></label>
<p class="span-full">The Control Plane has no global execution cap. Lowering a limit does not cancel already accepted work; new requests wait for capacity.</p>
<div class="field span-full"><label for="endpoint">Local Docker endpoint</label><input id="endpoint" name="dockerEndpoint" value="@Model.Policy.DockerEndpoint" required /></div><div class="form-actions"><button class="button primary" type="submit">Save Agent policy</button></div></form></section>
<div class="notice warning">Host execution is a separate capability: enable it in operational policy and explicitly deploy compose.agent.privileged.yaml together with compose.agent.yaml on the Agent host. This grants host-root command execution; this form alone cannot grant host kernel capabilities.</div><a href="/agents">← Agents</a>
